{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Arise, in the transgressions of my enemies</b> — On account of their transgressions, rise against them in Your anger. Some say: Anger them until they have transgressions. Some say: Exalt Yourself in the passing of my enemies." "R. Moses said: <b>and awake for me</b> — awaken for me justice, for You decreed that the kingdom of Saul would turn to me, for Saul, according to his opinion, is Cush or Peleth, to mention him by his known name. And Ben Balaam said: Awaken what You decreed to deliver me. And according to the opinion of these, <b>and awake</b> would be of the verbs that go out [transitively] in the manner of the word שב, which sometimes goes out [transitively] and sometimes stands [intransitively]. But the correct one in my eyes is that <b>and awake for me</b> — is a standing [intransitive] word, and a kaf of the construction is missing, like ועיר פרא אדם יולד. And when you hear <b>congregation of peoples</b>, [it means] the justice that You performed — let them come from the ends of the earth, and this is the meaning of <b>surround You</b>." "And the meaning of <b>and upon it to the height return</b> — that He return to the heavens to sit on the throne of justice; therefore after it, <b>YHWH judges peoples</b>. This too is correct, for the people of Cush were servants among the nations and surrounded David as though they surrounded the Shekhinah, for he is the servant of HaShem and takes refuge in Him, as he mentioned at the beginning of the psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:34.606349121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}